60
00:02:43.030 --> 00:02:44.710
Fast Facts number one.

61
00:02:45.070 --> 00:02:49.890
This was our season premiere and also Steve Carell's last season.

62
00:02:50.210 --> 00:02:55.470
Like we said last week, before season six ended, the cast and crew knew that this would

63
00:02:55.470 --> 00:03:01.790
be his last season, but the news was officially announced publicly over the summer break, and

64
00:03:01.790 --> 00:03:03.650
there were a lot of opinions about it.

65
00:03:03.910 --> 00:03:04.590
Oh, yeah.

66
00:03:05.250 --> 00:03:08.310
Mostly people were saying that The Office would be dead without Steve.

67
00:03:08.590 --> 00:03:08.770
Yeah.

68
00:03:08.770 --> 00:03:13.510
This news also put a lot of focus on our season premiere episode.

69
00:03:13.770 --> 00:03:19.570
In fact, it was seen by 8.4 million viewers, which was a big bump from our season six finale

70
00:03:19.570 --> 00:03:21.350
of 6.6 million.

71
00:03:21.570 --> 00:03:24.330
So almost two more million people tuned in.

72
00:03:24.510 --> 00:03:25.610
That's a lot.

73
00:03:25.770 --> 00:03:26.130
I know.

74
00:03:26.890 --> 00:03:32.450
The writers spent a lot of time over the summer talking about how to craft Steve's last season.

75
00:03:33.050 --> 00:03:36.850
Their big question was, why does Michael leave Dunder Mifflin?

76
00:03:36.850 --> 00:03:39.070
Yeah, because he loves Dunder Mifflin.

77
00:03:39.170 --> 00:03:39.770
It's his family.

78
00:03:40.050 --> 00:03:40.430
Exactly.

79
00:03:41.150 --> 00:03:45.270
Well, Paul Lieberstein said one thing they discussed was Michael getting fired at the

80
00:03:45.270 --> 00:03:45.550
end.

81
00:03:45.710 --> 00:03:49.970
And we had set this up a little bit with the problems with Saber and the printers.

82
00:03:49.970 --> 00:03:52.490
He'd become kind of like the spokesperson.

83
00:03:52.950 --> 00:03:53.230
Right.

84
00:03:53.450 --> 00:03:57.790
So there was discussion like maybe that was all going to cave in and he'd have to leave.

85
00:03:58.030 --> 00:03:58.250
Yeah.

86
00:03:58.330 --> 00:04:00.110
He'd be the fall guy for Saber.

87
00:04:00.110 --> 00:04:00.630
Yes.

88
00:04:01.190 --> 00:04:05.450
But ultimately, they thought that was like not doing right by Michael Scott.

89
00:04:05.950 --> 00:04:08.930
They decided that they really wanted him to grow.

90
00:04:09.210 --> 00:04:10.830
They wanted him to find love.

91
00:04:11.050 --> 00:04:14.210
They wanted him to have a really positive and iconic goodbye.

92
00:04:14.950 --> 00:04:18.010
So I listened to the DVD commentary for this episode.

93
00:04:18.530 --> 00:04:22.970
By the way, you guys, I have a whole story about what it took for me just to watch a DVD.

94
00:04:23.270 --> 00:04:24.330
It was a journey.

95
00:04:24.510 --> 00:04:24.850
Amazing.

96
00:04:24.970 --> 00:04:25.930
Because you were in Texas.

97
00:04:25.930 --> 00:04:26.350
Yes.

98
00:04:26.470 --> 00:04:27.410
Visiting your family.

99
00:04:27.410 --> 00:04:29.330
Yeah, in a very small town.

100
00:04:29.590 --> 00:04:34.190
Anyway, I will save that because we have so much to cover, but I have to share later.

101
00:04:34.930 --> 00:04:37.230
Anyway, so I finally was able to watch this DVD.

102
00:04:37.570 --> 00:04:43.050
It featured Craig Robinson, Creed Bratton, writers Danny Chun, BJ Novak, and Paul Lieberstein.

103
00:04:43.550 --> 00:04:48.050
Danny, BJ, and Paul talked about this being Michael's last season and how they wanted to

104
00:04:48.050 --> 00:04:49.550
approach storylines for him.

105
00:04:49.670 --> 00:04:51.850
And I found this conversation so interesting.

106
00:04:51.970 --> 00:04:53.930
Jenna, we love the whole writers process.

107
00:04:54.150 --> 00:04:54.490
Oh, yeah.

108
00:04:54.690 --> 00:04:55.130
We love it.

109
00:04:55.130 --> 00:05:00.430
And they shared that this episode kicked off a change in Michael because his co-workers

110
00:05:00.430 --> 00:05:01.330
were his family.

111
00:05:01.670 --> 00:05:07.370
And him bringing his actual nephew, his actual family into the office, he has to try to figure

112
00:05:07.370 --> 00:05:09.310
out how to separate work from family.

113
00:05:10.230 --> 00:05:14.390
And they also said that they just wanted to show Michael's growth as a person.

114
00:05:14.810 --> 00:05:16.270
Here, they say it better than I do.

115
00:05:16.370 --> 00:05:16.830
Let's listen.

116
00:05:17.510 --> 00:05:22.090
You know, telling Michael that's mixing business and family, these are his two favorite things.

117
00:05:22.370 --> 00:05:22.670
Right.

118
00:05:22.990 --> 00:05:25.730
So he, of all people, would not see the problem here.

119
00:05:26.110 --> 00:05:27.370
Just couldn't understand.

120
00:05:27.850 --> 00:05:33.370
And this was kind of, this came about from us talking about Steve's last season and what

121
00:05:33.370 --> 00:05:39.270
are the stories that are kind of quintessential Michael's stories that we just never told.

122
00:05:40.070 --> 00:05:45.190
Um, and we were able to kind of have him grow in a way that he wasn't, he didn't.

123
00:05:45.190 --> 00:05:51.230
Yeah, the whole season we would approach Michael finally, um, letting Michael have grown

124
00:05:51.230 --> 00:05:53.950
a bit by the end of an episode, which we generally never did.

125
00:05:55.830 --> 00:05:57.150
Setting him off in style.

126
00:05:57.930 --> 00:05:58.290
Yeah.

127
00:05:58.490 --> 00:05:59.190
Because we, you know.

128
00:05:59.290 --> 00:06:02.130
We wanted him to be like a more of a whole person by the time he left.

129
00:06:02.270 --> 00:06:03.910
Yeah, we knew more or less how he was going to leave.

130
00:06:03.910 --> 00:06:10.410
Even, yeah, often, uh, up till, up till this season, Michael would just find a new level

131
00:06:10.410 --> 00:06:13.170
of denial to end a episode.

132
00:06:13.450 --> 00:06:13.590
Right, right.

133
00:06:13.790 --> 00:06:14.830
And that would be funny.

134
00:06:15.250 --> 00:06:15.410
Yeah.

135
00:06:15.670 --> 00:06:22.750
Um, but we could start firing off our, our Michael self-awareness gun because we knew we only

136
00:06:22.750 --> 00:06:23.510
had a few bullets anyway.

137
00:06:24.890 --> 00:06:25.450
Mm-hmm.

138
00:06:25.670 --> 00:06:25.850
Yeah.

139
00:06:26.030 --> 00:06:33.890
I remember that, that there was this just overall idea of Michael growing into a man that

140
00:06:33.890 --> 00:06:37.610
could leave and marry Holly because they knew that was the end.

141
00:06:37.750 --> 00:06:38.470
That was the goal.

142
00:06:38.610 --> 00:06:38.850
Yes.

143
00:06:39.070 --> 00:06:41.550
But we only had one season to get him there now.

144
00:06:41.670 --> 00:06:41.970
Right.

145
00:06:42.110 --> 00:06:47.270
And it is interesting now as we rewatch this whole season seven, you are going to see Michael

146
00:06:47.270 --> 00:06:52.070
becoming more self-aware, more aware of his actions and how they affect other people.

147
00:06:52.630 --> 00:06:53.290
Really cool.

148
00:06:53.890 --> 00:06:54.270
All right.

